PLACEHOLDER — Sparkle Ed25519 (EdDSA) public key slot. Not a real key yet.

Sparkle 2 signs update feeds with an ed25519 keypair (SPEC §6; T9). This file
is where the PUBLIC key gets recorded once generated — the public key is not
secret and may be committed after signing week. The PRIVATE key never leaves
the macOS Keychain of the release machine.

Keygen is a signing-week HUMAN step (full walkthrough in scripts/README.md,
section "Sparkle Ed25519 keys"):

  1. Build the app once (so Sparkle's tools are in DerivedData), then:
       find ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData -name generate_keys -type f
  2. Run that binary — it prints the public key and stores the private key in
     your login Keychain.
  3. Record the public key here, AND pass it to release builds via
     SCRIBE_PUBLIC_ED_KEY (scripts/release.sh bakes it into Info.plist
     SUPublicEDKey).

Until then SUPUBLIC_ED_KEY in project.yml stays empty — update verification
stays disabled, which is fine for local and CI builds.
